# Toronto Rising — hide / restore objects (mandatory)

**Every off-table park at `y = C.HIDDEN_OBJECT_WORLD_Y` (-200) must go through `O.hideObject` / `O.restoreObject`.** Do not hand-roll `setPosition({ y = -200 })`, parallel lock/interactable toggles, or inline `setInvisibleTo({...})` for hide/reveal flows.

Canonical doc: [`docs/solutions/lua-hide-restore-policy.md`](../../docs/solutions/lua-hide-restore-policy.md).

## The pair

| API | Module | Object scripts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hide | `O.hideObject(obj, opts?)` | `Global.call("GlobalHideObject", { guid, parkPosition?, parkRotation?, snapshotPosition? })` |
| Restore | `O.restoreObject(obj, opts?)` | `Global.call("GlobalRestoreObject", { guid, position?, rotation?, locked?, interactable? })` |

**Source:** `core/objects.ttslua`. **Constant:** `C.HIDDEN_OBJECT_WORLD_Y`. **Snapshot:** `gameState.hiddenObjects[guid]`.

## What hide applies (only here)

Park Y, `setLock(true)`, `interactable = false`, parked visibility (all viewer colors), `HiddenObject` tag. Snapshot stores `invisibleTo` (not parked Y when already at −200).

**What restore applies (only here)**

Caller opts → catalogs (`C.LockedObjects`) → snapshot fallback; active visibility: **`C.HiddenObjects[guid]` when catalogued** → snapshot `invisibleTo` → `{}`. Clears tag and snapshot.

**Do not** hard-code player color arrays at call sites (use catalog + snapshot). For on-table re-apply without unparking, use `O.applyActiveVisibility(obj)`.

## Options table

**Hide:** `parkPosition`, `parkRotation`, `snapshotPosition` (when live Y is already parked).

**Restore:** `position`, `rotation`, `locked`, `interactable` — prefer explicit `position` when restore authority is a catalog pose, table home, or board UV, not the snapshot alone.

## Helpers

- `O.isHiddenObject(obj)` — guard / idempotency
- `O.activeVisibilityForGuid(guid)` — active-mode visibility from `C.HiddenObjects` (never inline lists)
- `O.applyActiveVisibility(obj)` — apply catalog active visibility on an on-table object
- `O.noteHiddenObjectWorldXZ(obj)` — layout moved hidden satellite X/Z
- `O.transferHideSnapshot(fromGuid, toGuid)` — multi-state figurines

## Object scripts

**Never** `require("core.objects")` from object-hosted scripts — use `GlobalHideObject` / `GlobalRestoreObject` (see [toronto-rising-object-script-bundling.mdc](toronto-rising-object-script-bundling.mdc)).

## Documented exceptions (do not migrate blindly)

- Startup `C.HiddenObjects` visibility-only apply (present seats at authored Y)
- Secret roll dice invisibility helpers
- Seat-layout NPC chair visibility only (`enforceNPCSeatObjectVisibility`) — not preload pool hide
- Spotlight phase seat figurines (`SEAT_FIGURE_*`) — stay at seats; active visibility via `O.applyActiveVisibility` / `O.restoreObject` from `C.HiddenObjects` (never `O.hideObject` park, never blanket PC hide lists)

New exceptions must be added to `docs/solutions/lua-hide-restore-policy.md`.

## Agent checklist (before marking hide/reveal work done)

1. Grep edited files for `-200`, `setInvisibleTo({`, and manual lock+Y stash patterns — migrate or document exception.
2. Object scripts → Global.call, not `require("core.*")`.
3. Restore passes explicit `position` when catalog/computed pose is authoritative.
4. New Global mutators → row in [Event Listener Policy](../../.dev/Sychronizing%20Game%20Functionality/Event%20Listener%20Policy.md).
